   GeoShake Seismic Network, https://map.geoshake.org
   (accessed YYYY-MM-DD), CC BY 4.0

If you use the data in a publication we would like to hear about it:
https://geoshake.org/contact


STATION LOCATIONS AND PRIVACY
-----------------------------

Station coordinates are chosen by the station operator during setup, not
collected automatically. Operators are told at that point that the
station map is public and that an approximate position is sufficient —
many deliberately offset the pin from their exact address.

Treat published coordinates as approximate. Do not attempt to use them
to identify, locate or contact the residents of a station, and do not
combine them with other datasets for that purpose.

If you are a station operator and want your station's position changed
or removed, contact https://geoshake.org/contact


WHAT THIS DATA IS - AND IS NOT
------------------------------

Please represent the data accurately in any work based on it:

- Sensors are consumer-grade MEMS accelerometers. They are NOT
  calibrated, and no instrument response is published. Station metadata
  is therefore provided only down to station level - no channel response
  is available.
- Amplitudes are indicative, not metrologically traceable. Do not treat
  them as equivalent to a calibrated seismometer.
- The network code currently published in StationXML, SAC and SeedLink
  is PROVISIONAL and not yet registered with the FDSN. It will change
  once a code is assigned.
- Event detections are produced by an automatic algorithm. They are not
  reviewed by a seismologist and may contain false positives and missed
  events.
- Station coverage is uneven and changes continuously as operators join
  and leave.


NO WARRANTY - NOT A SAFETY SYSTEM
---------------------------------

The data is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability
and fitness for a particular purpose.

GeoShake is a community monitoring network, NOT an official earthquake
early warning service and NOT a substitute for one. Do not use this data
or these services as the sole basis for life-safety, evacuation,
structural, insurance or emergency-response decisions. Always follow the
guidance of your national seismological and civil protection authorities.

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Appflows Teknoloji
A.S. accepts no liability for any loss or damage arising from use of, or
reliance on, this data.


SERVICE AVAILABILITY
--------------------

The data is openly licensed, but the services that deliver it are
operated on a best-effort basis with no uptime guarantee. Endpoints may
be rate-limited, changed or withdrawn. Heavy or automated use should go
through https://geoshake.org/developer so we can keep the service usable
for everyone.

